    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42295" root="وكث" body-key="w">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وِكَاثٌ</span></b>  and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وُكَاثٌ</span> <i>Food, aliment,</i> or <i>nutriment,</i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غِذَآءٌ</span>: so in some copies of the K, and in
the TA: in the CK, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غَدَآءٌ</span>, or <i>a morning meal:</i>)
<i>that is prepared,</i> or <i>taken, in haste,</i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">يُسْتَعْجَلُ بِهِ</span>,)
[<i>before the morning-meal called</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غَدَآء</span>: see 10].
(K.)

